From 8768053fd23f31719a90f8b2d08628dc97e4a311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:44:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(sim): carry the machined body into the next setup

The program sim no longer refuses a program that spans setups holding
the part differently. On entering such a setup (or one placed relative
to the previous with #316's link), the body the earlier setups left is
carried through setup_relative::transform_between: a two-sided column
body (top and floor per column) re-indexed exactly onto the image
lattice for flips over X/Y and quarter turns about Z - never
re-sampled (#308). After a flip the floor is judged against the part's
bottom, so a gouge cut before the flip is still a gouge after it.
Same-held unlinked setups keep the M3.2 A clip. Turns the lattice
cannot carry exactly, and lathe/mill-turn machines, refuse by name.
stock_sim::incoming_body exposes a setup's incoming stock for #318 and
#320.

Fixes #317

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
